WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.880
With speculation swirling that Avengers: Endgame
will find Earth's Mightiest Heroes traveling

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.510
through time, there's no telling who they
might encounter along the way.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.390
No character from the Marvel Cinematic Universe
is off the table, so here's a look at some

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.720
dead MCU characters we might see in Avengers:
Endgame.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.300
Of all the characters in the rich history
of the MCU, Brock Rumlow probably wouldn't

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.040
be voted Most Likely to Return.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.199
But the villain known as Crossbones, who first
appeared in Captain America: The Winter Soldier

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.060
before dying in Captain America: Civil War,
seems to be making a comeback.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.580
Frank Grillo, who plays Crossbones, revealed
on the podcast UFC Unfiltered that he is indeed

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.920
returning in a flashback in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.920
Usually, Marvel keeps a tight lid on spoilers,
but as Grillo explained,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.020
"I'm allowed to say whatever I want because
I'm never doing another Marvel movie."

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.040
Another character fans expect to appear in
Avengers: Endgame is Captain America's one

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.560
true love, Peggy Carter.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.800
She's made a number of high profile appearances
in the MCU, from the 1940's through the present,

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.420
before passing away in Captain America: Civil
War.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.780
But in 2017 star Hayley Atwell stoked rumors
of a return to the MCU by posting a photo

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.880
on social media that seemed to be from the
set of Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.360
Considering Marvel made a point of including
her in the first Endgame trailer, it seems

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.960
possible the fan theory that Cap and Peggy
will be reunited may actually come true.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.520
One of the most talked about moments in Avengers:
Infinity War is the scene where Thanos communes

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.729
with the spirit of Gamora, the adopted daughter
he murdered earlier in the film.

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:35.260
It was later revealed that, as fans had guessed,
the reunion took place inside the Soul Stone,

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:39.049
which in the comics is known for storing the
spirits of dead heroes until they are ready

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:39.980
to be resurrected.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.959
So it seems like there's a pretty fair bet
that before Endgame is over, Gamora will be

00:01:44.959 --> 00:01:49.189
reborn, and considering the circumstances
surrounding her death, this is one father

00:01:49.189 --> 00:01:50.860
daughter dance we don't want to miss.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.780
Vision has already been brought back from
the dead once through the power of the time

00:01:55.789 --> 00:01:57.340
stone, so we know it's possible.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.120
Of course, he was then immediately killed
again, but as an artificial life form, even

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.509
if the Infinity Stones aren't involved it's
theoretically possible he could be rebuilt

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:06.920
by Shuri or Tony Stark.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.280
One way or another, his love story with Scarlet
Witch deserves a happier ending.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.060
Like Crossbones, Arnim Zola isn't an obvious
choice for resurrection.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.700
But we know Marvel's filmmakers have been
trying to get him back into the picture, as

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.110
he almost appeared in Ant-Man's '80s flashback.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.660
And there are two easy ways to get him in
the picture.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:28.870
Firstly, in Winter Soldier we saw that he
had achieved digital immortality by uploading

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:31.120
his consciousness to an old computer system.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.780
While that was destroyed, it would be super
easy to have backups.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.180
More interesting, though, is the fact that
Zola was alive and active as a Hydra mole

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.340
inside SHIELD for several decades after World
War II.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:47.060
That would make him a perfect villain to interact
with the Avengers if they go back in time,

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:51.460
and would also make it easy for his story
to intersect with a Peggy Carter appearance.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.040
Connect those dots, Marvel!

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.400
Another character active in the past is Black
Panther's father, King T'Chaka.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.780
Now that the Avengers know about Wakanda's
technological superiority, they could very

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.260
well contact T'Chaka for help in the past.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.700
But we could also see Black Panther himself.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.840
After all, we know that the monarchs of Wakanda
live on in a spiritual afterworld, ready to

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.240
guide those who come after.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.920
Whether it's Shuri or M'baku, whoever takes
the throne of Wakanda after T'Challa's death

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.200
may very well visit him in the afterlife.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.020
Even in death, the Black Panther protects
his people.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.380
The Asgardian God of Mischief has already
spent so much of his time in the MCU dying

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:30.360
and coming back.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.560
With all the times this greasy little possum
has faked out the audience, it's no surprise

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.150
that Thanos felt the need to declare that
Loki would get "no resurrections this time."

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.080
It also means we're not entirely ready to
believe him.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.640
And he's not the only dead Asgardian who could
make a comeback.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:48.740
Every single person in Thor's life is either
dead or missing.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:53.840
Having Odin, or Heimdall, or the long lost
Sif return would finally give the god of Thunder

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.600
a little hope among all this loss.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.560
Speaking of lost families, the members of
the Guardians of the Galaxy have been struggling

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.020
with their ghosts from day one.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.400
"Everybody's got dead people!

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.920
That's no excuse to get everybody else dead
along the way!"

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.900
With most of the Guardians now dead themselves,
the stage could be set for some more reunions

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.980
in the afterlife of the Soul Stone.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:20.880
Drax's wife and child, Peter's mom, Gamora's
real parents, they're all possibilities in

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.400
Endgame.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.860
Perhaps the most important lost family in
the MCU, though, are Tony Stark's parents

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:27.860
Howard and Maria.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.510
Tony's fraught relationship with Howard was
the focal point of Iron Man 2, and the circumstances

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.920
behind their death drove the plot of Captain
America: Civil War.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.360
Considering many people expect Endgame to
be the final chapter in Tony's story, it would

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:45.140
be thematically appropriate and emotionally
satisfying if Tony and his parents were reunited.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.790
Perhaps even more important, though, is the
fact that Howard Stark is a co-founder of

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:53.140
SHIELD, and thus the spiritual father of the
Avengers themselves.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.380
Considering the credits for Endgame strongly
hint that some part of the film takes place

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:02.780
in the 1970's, it's very possible we may see
Howard and Tony Stark team up to defeat Thanos

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:03.320
together.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:11.160
"What is and always will be my greatest creation
is you."

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:15.940
It got a little tough to keep track of everything
that was happening in Age of Ultron.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.020
Remember Quicksilver?

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:19.360
Scarlet Witch's brother, Pietro Maximoff?

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:24.260
He ran really fast and died protecting Clint
Barton from a hail of bullets as Sokovia fell

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.000
from the sky.

00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:29.220
It's easy to forget, though, since even his
sister hasn't mentioned him in the years since

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:29.720
his death.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.660
But that doesn't mean he's been completely
forgotten.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:35.920
With Disney's acquisition of Fox opening the
door to the addition of the X-Men and their

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:40.460
version of Quicksilver to the MCU, bringing
back Marvel's version of Quicksilver might

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:45.020
be an interesting and unexpected way to begin
that transition into the next phase of the

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.460
Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.740
No matter what Marvel tells us, we all know
that not all of those deaths in the climax

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.610
of Infinity War were permanent.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:58.340
Heck, Marvel has already announced films featuring
a number of dead characters, including Spider-Man:

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:02.400
Far from Home, which is slated to open less
than three months after Endgame.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.900
It's not a question of if we'll see the return
of Spider-Man, Black Panther and Doctor Strange,

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.500
it's just a matter of how.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:10.120
We can't wait to find out.

